n  you wrote my last Christmas at home and  I was put out of the house butt-naked at  gunpoint till this day I still have a  problem with Christmas but I made a  decision that I was going to be  everything that this guy was not I'm not  going to drink and I'm not going to beat  women I'm not going to be ignorant and  one of the tactics that I developed as a  young kid I would read and I'd read out  loud and I would be saying to this guy  yeah you can beat me down you can beat  me you can beat my mom you can put us  out of here  with a gun but I can read and I'm going  places this man whose own father had  abandoned him found himself carrying his  plans into the office of Nelson Mandela  you walked into his office he looked at  you and said welcome home son  I had to be 46 years old and for the  first time in my life a man ever to say  the words to me welcome home son and for  it to be Nelson Mandela I cried I cried  I asked myself when I was trying to  compose my thoughts what would I want to  hear from someone today what I want to  hear more about the state of the economy  Wall Street bailouts of a job market no  I would like to hear from someone that  you know what amidst all this chaos and  turbulence there's an opportunity to  create a new vision of the American  dream that's what I would like to hear  from somebody today our new vision of  the American Dream as great as any of  the visions that dreams of our  forefathers founding fathers and  ancestors a new vision of the American  Dream that says achieving balance in  your life is more important than the  balance in your checking account  new vision a new vision of the Americans  rainwear appreciation is greater than  expectation a new vision that says for  too long a lot of us been living in  exile in a place called things and it's  time for us to come home to France  families and folks  I submit to you today that this new  vision of the American Dream means that  what you do does not define who you are  a ne